{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 102, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a none on edge 4 in a disconnected cell (exp 92) gives a huge gain, while upgrading an existing op gives small changes."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Connecting the output edge from none (exp 93) yields +24 to +76 points, versus a few points for replacing existing ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring a path to the output node from none (exp 99) gives massive gains compared to swapping existing ops."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a direct input-to-output path where edge 3 was none gives large gains (exps 77, 100) versus small or negative effects otherwise."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a conv3x3 into the output hurts across datasets (exps 3, 53, 73), whereas removing weak ops (skip/avg_pool) in a weak cell helps."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a skip_connect on edge 5 helps in the all-skip parent (+42/+39/+10) and in exp 83, unlike removing conv ops."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a skip_connect on edge 4 to a conv yields large gains (exps 25, 35), while replacing conv3x3 with conv1x1 is neutral or negative."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Dropping edge 3 in a skip-dominated cell is much less harmful (+28 in exp 27) than in conv-heavy cells where it costs up to -16 on I